{"type":"assistant","uuid":"a99bbcb0-d91f-4f3f-8ac9-bbf43963bb9b","session_id":"6823368e-7d30-41de-8a9a-fadd61843571","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"a99bbcb0-d91f-4f3f-8ac9-bbf43963bb9b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is verified. Here's a summary:\n\n---\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n### Root Cause\nIn `DocumentEditFragment.onResume()`, the editor's text was being reset unconditionally every time the fragment resumed (when switching back to the app), without preserving the cursor position:\n\n```java\n@Override\npublic void onResume() {\n    super.onResume();\n    checkReloadDisk();\n    _hlEditor.setText(_document.getContent());  // <-- resets cursor to 0\n}\n```\n\nWhen `setText()` is called on an EditText, Android resets the selection/cursor to position 0 (the beginning). This happens every time the user switches away and back, or opens a dialog like \"insert image\" that causes the fragment to pause and resume.\n\n### Fix\nSave the cursor position before `setText()`, clamp it to the new text length, and restore it after — following the same pattern already used in `loadDocumentIntoUi()`:\n\n```diff\n     public void onResume() {\n         super.onResume();\n         checkReloadDisk();\n+        int cursorPos = _hlEditor.getSelectionStart();\n         _hlEditor.setText(_document.getContent());\n+        cursorPos = cursorPos > _hlEditor.length() ? _hlEditor.length() - 1 : cursorPos;\n+        _hlEditor.setSelection(cursorPos < 0 ? 0 : cursorPos);\n     }\n```\n\n### Verification\n- Build completed successfully (`BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 41s`, 84 tasks executed)\n- The fix is minimal and follows the existing pattern in `loadDocumentIntoUi()` (lines 138-140), which already handles cursor preservation correctly"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42709,"output_tokens":376,"cache_read_input_tokens":41184,"total_tokens":43085}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"5490d4fb-acff-4600-98d2-50220ffb245e","session_id":"6823368e-7d30-41de-8a9a-fadd61843571","is_error":false,"duration_ms":141626,"duration_api_ms":97580,"num_turns":17,"result":"The fix is verified. Here's a summary:\n\n---\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n### Root Cause\nIn `DocumentEditFragment.onResume()`, the editor's text was being reset unconditionally every time the fragment resumed (when switching back to the app), without preserving the cursor position:\n\n```java\n@Override\npublic void onResume() {\n    super.onResume();\n    checkReloadDisk();\n    _hlEditor.setText(_document.getContent());  // <-- resets cursor to 0\n}\n```\n\nWhen `setText()` is called on an EditText, Android resets the selection/cursor to position 0 (the beginning). This happens every time the user switches away and back, or opens a dialog like \"insert image\" that causes the fragment to pause and resume.\n\n### Fix\nSave the cursor position before `setText()`, clamp it to the new text length, and restore it after — following the same pattern already used in `loadDocumentIntoUi()`:\n\n```diff\n     public void onResume() {\n         super.onResume();\n         checkReloadDisk();\n+        int cursorPos = _hlEditor.getSelectionStart();\n         _hlEditor.setText(_document.getContent());\n+        cursorPos = cursorPos > _hlEditor.length() ? _hlEditor.length() - 1 : cursorPos;\n+        _hlEditor.setSelection(cursorPos < 0 ? 0 : cursorPos);\n     }\n```\n\n### Verification\n- Build completed successfully (`BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 41s`, 84 tasks executed)\n- The fix is minimal and follows the existing pattern in `loadDocumentIntoUi()` (lines 138-140), which already handles cursor preservation correctly","usage":{"input_tokens":627672,"output_tokens":5674,"cache_read_input_tokens":553344,"total_tokens":633346},"permission_denials":[]}
